# Copy to .env and adjust. Expo only exposes variables prefixed
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ to app code (see src/config/env.ts) — this is required by
# Expo, not optional.
#
# IMPORTANT: "localhost" here means the phone/emulator itself, NOT your
# development machine. Pick the value for your actual test target:
#
#   Android emulator  -> http://10.0.2.2:8000        (emulator's alias for the host machine)
#   iOS simulator     -> http://127.0.0.1:8000        (simulator shares the Mac's network namespace)
#   Physical device   -> http://<your-machine-LAN-IP>:8000   (e.g. http://192.168.1.23:8000 — phone
#                         and dev machine must be on the same Wi-Fi network; find your IP with
#                         `ipconfig` (Windows) / `ifconfig` or `ipconfig getifaddr en0` (macOS))
#   Production        -> https://your-real-api-domain.example.com  (never commit a real value here)
#
# The FastAPI backend must also have this origin/IP reachable and CORS_ORIGINS
# in backend/.env does not need to include it (CORS only applies to browser
# clients; a React Native app is not subject to browser CORS enforcement).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8000
